{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-CUTOVER FINDINGS 'A' CAPTURED, on a real Gerrit change reviewed by the production bot on the ANTHROPIC path. This is the first half of the pre/post comparison criterion, and it is recorded BEFORE the cutover so the comparison cannot be assembled after the fact.\n\nTHE FIXTURE. Gerrit change 1325 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1325), the fix for [rebar:4e71-f237-28c4-4c65] (bedrock_model.py naming AWS_REGION as a remedy when it does not resolve). It is pushed and DELIBERATELY NOT SUBMITTED — held open across the cutover precisely so the same change can be re-reviewed afterwards. Change-Id Iedec756aef732226e97416cb1f6ebcfc281ade31, revision a46d856c72dae0c6fc8db36.\n\nTHE VOTE, from Gerrit's own message log:\n    rebar-review-bot @ 2026-08-03 23:15:31 — 'Patch Set 1: LLM-Review+1  [LLM-Review: PASS]  rebar code review passed.'\nLabels now: LLM-Review=+1, Verified=0 (CI still running), Code-Review=0.\n\nTHE ARTIFACT. code_review ticket 1aa5-1574-50be-4e65, titled 'code-review: Iedec756aef732226e97416cb1f6ebcfc281ade31 @ a46d856c72dae0c6fc8db36'. From its REVIEW_RESULT sidecar:\n    provider_provenance = {\"provider\": \"anthropic\", \"model\": \"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n                           \"tier\": \"first_class\", \"endpoint_host\": null,\n                           \"capabilities\": {\"prompt_cache_style\": \"anthropic\",\n                                            \"native_structured_output\": false,\n                                            \"supports_temperature\": true, \"supports_thinking\": true}}\n    model    = claude-opus-4-8            (the frontier pass; the provenance names the STANDARD class from the verify step)\n    blocking = 0 items\n    advisory = 0 items\n    dropped  = 0 items\n\nWHY A ZERO-FINDING BASELINE IS THE STRONGEST ONE AVAILABLE for this criterion. The criterion asks that the same change reviewed pre- and post-cutover yields comparable findings, with 'no new blocking finding that is an artifact of the provider'. With A at zero blocking, ANY blocking finding in B is unambiguously new — there is no judgement call about whether a finding 'corresponds' to a pre-existing one, which is exactly where a comparison of two non-empty finding lists would get soft. The cost is that a zero-vs-zero comparison says little about finding QUALITY; that is accepted, and it is consistent with the operator's standing scope ruling that comparing models against one another is out of scope and that verdict agreement is informational rather than a gate.\n\nHOW B WILL BE OBTAINED, stated now so the method is fixed in advance: post-cutover, '/rerun' this SAME change so the SAME revision is re-reviewed, then read the same three finding lists and the same provenance key from the new artifact. The expectation is provider == 'bedrock', model == 'bedrock:us.anthropic.*', capabilities.prompt_cache_style off 'anthropic', and blocking still 0. Comparing the same revision is what makes it a provider comparison rather than a content comparison.\n\nA NOTE ON THE DRILL TRIGGER, since it interacts with this. The induced-VOTER_ERROR drill needs a real webhook, i.e. a push. I will NOT use a new patchset on 1325 as that trigger if it would leave A and B on different revisions — if a patchset 2 becomes the drill trigger, then A is re-taken on patchset 2 after the gate is restored, so A and B are always the same revision. The bot is confirmed healthy and actively voting (/health reports in_flight=2, voter_voted events landing), so the current absence of a vote on 1326 is queue depth, not a stuck gate — and the drill will not be started while any change of mine is awaiting its first review."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785799052306508001,"uuid":"2d2153c8-964d-4b78-bc58-2436dad00c56"}